WEBVTT

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.170
Oh right, I was cooking.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.890
Like this?

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.640
There! It tastes better this way
than eating it plain.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.060
But it's a shame he doesn't know
anything about cooking.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.690
Riri will have to teach him.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.610
Oh yeah, Mushicchi!

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.740
Could you go get some water?

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.620
IT'S NUSHI, NOT MUSHI.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.040
Whatever. You look like a bug.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.330
Don't worry, Riri likes bugs.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:44.870
Thanks.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.170
Maybe I should go ahead and eat.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.550
When will he come home?

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.300
Leaving cute little Riri behind
and working all day like this.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:05.100
I love the feel of Kemurikusa.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.060
Fuzzy, fluffy...

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:14.650
Oh, another one that
only grown-ups can use. Darn.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.780
But that means
I have so much more I can learn.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.500
He's back! Hey!

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.710
Wakaba!

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.130
Welcome back, Wakaba.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.680
I'm home, Riri.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.800
You're late.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:44.470
Sorry, it took a while to grow a new one.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.640
I bet it's about Kemurikusa again.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.730
You see right through me.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.190
I've cooked for us.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.940
Great, I can't wait.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.410
I lightly seared the Usuiro today.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.450
Wow, that's an interesting way to eat it.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:05.000
I also made some tea.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.170
I wonder how everything will taste.
I totally can't wait.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.920
That was great.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.880
You have to enjoy eating.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.130
We don't look at the meaning too much.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.970
It's an interesting culture.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.930
That's right, Mushicchi helped out too.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.810
Thanks, you're a great help.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.680
CAPTAIN, GIVE ME ORDER.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:32.020
Then could you check to see
if the island I just made is okay?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:33.940
ADMINISTRATION, COLOR, DETECTED.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.320
Tell Nushiji and Nushizo too.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.240
Do Mushicchi and the others
run on Kemurikusa too?

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:43.280
That's right.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.240
They think and act on their own,

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.960
but they need orders
and Kemurikusa for important decisions.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.590
Oh, this was invented recently.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.800
It's such a pretty color.
And this leaf, I really like the sound.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.260
You really like Kemurikusa, don't you?

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.680
Sorry, I was talking fast again, wasn't I?

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.690
I like watching you talk about Kemurikusa.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.190
It must be complicated and boring.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.900
No, I've learned a lot already.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.400
Really? It's not easy.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:18.650
No, I get it.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.200
Push hard, and when circles come up...

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:27.580
Standard use, strength,
lock, and release.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.160
You know so much...

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.750
Look what else.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.260
Huh? How did you do that?
Did you just mix two leaves?

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:42.180
Yeah, you can connect them
by making them the same color.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.180
They work from top to bottom.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.720
Wow, I never knew that.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.100
-You're a genius!
-You bet!

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:55.020
It must be the good eyesight, memory,
and curiosity of earthlings.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.150
Can I try this one too?

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.780
Oh yeah, Riri.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.410
Never use Kemurikusa on other people.
And only eat Usuiro.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.370
Because it'll hurt them?

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.200
Not just hurt them. People are complex.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.460
You never know what'll happen.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.460
It could partly alter them,
or make them lose their memory.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:20.170
There was one case where
the brain's information was replicated.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.180
But recent colors might be able
to overcome that...

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.810
Sorry, I'm scaring you, aren't I?
A researcher's bad habit.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.930
Yeah, it really is a bad habit!

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.900
Don't worry, they're made
so you can't use them on people.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.860
But what about the green one
you once used on me?

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.110
That one can be used on people.
It can heal injuries.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.990
Nushicchi? Yeah.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:50.450
Oh no, this is bad.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.620
Sorry, Riri. I have to go back.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.250
Aww, you've done enough today.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.960
Sorry, but I have to
finish printing it today.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.090
Then Riri's coming with you.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.470
Well, I guess it wouldn't hurt
once in a while.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.300
Yay!

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.650
Off we go!

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.700
Together with Wakaba.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:36.540
Only grown-ups are allowed
to work with large Kemurikusa, but...

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.120
Too late now.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.550
That's the one
you printed the other day, right?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.010
How large is the one you're doing now?

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:54.310
The one I'm doing now
is taller than it is spacious.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.890
It's pretty complex, so it's difficult.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.440
But it's rewarding.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.240
Wow, it really is big!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.580
Okay, let's get to work.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.260
Nushizo, a bit to the right.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.560
It's looking pretty good.

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:43.320
Yeah, I don't think
it'll crumble this time.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:46.230
Are you going to do another city's worth?

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.860
Yes, as long as the leaves last.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:53.370
If they're fine after I dry them,
I'll be done for now.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.200
Your job is pretty strange.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.250
The progress of
a planet's cultural assets.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.580
I don't know much about it,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:06.170
but I was called because
they need large, precise Kemurikusa.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:10.180
I can research Kemurikusa
and learn about them while I work.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:13.050
I'm grateful for this job.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:17.140
So Earth is under this ship, right?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.350
That's right.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.140
It's too big, I don't get it.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.650
Yeah, I've never done any
this huge before either.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:30.150
But it's like growing
a really big Kemurikusa.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.370
Something growing is a wonderful thing.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.410
So I came out like this too?

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:43.000
Yeah, you really surprised me.
At that big lake.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.590
You suddenly came up out of the water.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:49.550
But living things don't get copied...

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:52.340
I died once, right?

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.890
Yeah, but I'm really glad you were saved.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.680
But you'll get in trouble.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:01.180
Yeah, the people on the planet
aren't supposed to know.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.060
But oh well. It's never happened before.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.480
Yeah, it's okay. I think...

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.940
Do you want to go back?

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.780
You must know lots of people on Earth.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:17.030
No. Mom and Dad are gone anyway.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:22.370
If everyone thinks I'm dead,
I want to stay here and help you.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.620
Thanks. You're a great help.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:29.300
Besides, I'm more worried about you.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.510
You're clumsy and too nice.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.380
Yeah, I get that a lot.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.470
Okay, let's finish this.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.220
Hey, don't touch that!

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.640
The color is going bad here.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.390
You're right... I mean, don't touch!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.360
Or I'll talk about
a person who became a ghost.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:52.900
Thanks. I'm surprised
the precision really improved.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:57.370
I'm a great help, huh?
Aren't I good enough to be a grown-up?

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:59.780
Well, not quite yet.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:04.790
Not again!

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:08.630
That stinks!
Stop smoking cigarettes all the time.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.630
I don't know what cigarettes are.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.590
But I'm tuning my body with Midori.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.640
It restores my original functions
and strengthens me.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.560
It definitely looks like a cigarette.
It's smelly!

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.310
It crumbled again.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.560
It becomes destroyed whenever
there isn't enough water circulating.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:31.690
Oops.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:35.740
Wakaba, you haven't been sleeping enough.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.780
It's fine.
We don't need as much sleep as you.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:40.740
But...

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.830
It's a precious cultural asset.
I have to print it before it's gone.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.580
Who cares?

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:51.250
Is that what you really want to do?

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:56.420
Well, I do wish
I could spend more time researching.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:00.600
If you keep this up, you'll die too...

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.930
Anyways, stop doing everything for others!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.440
You have to care for yourself too.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:10.520
You're such a good girl.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.110
Gosh.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.780
Don't worry.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:17.530
I only have to work until
the Kemurikusa's limit.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.700
It won't last long.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.990
If it stops,
you don't have to work anymore?

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.120
That's right.
It will take a bit more time, though.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.380
Mom and Dad worked too hard and...

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:42.100
I don't want to go through that again.
If Wakaba dies too...

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.850
The Kemurikusa's limit?

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:48.690
I know!

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.770
I'll make a Kemurikusa
that can stop Kemurikusa.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:56.570
That way, Wakaba won't have to
work as much.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:00.150
There! This should do it.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.200
I need to go get water for this tree.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:16.300
Inside the dark my heartbeat echoes

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:23.180
Long night will continue on

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:26.760
Time to face the hell that surrounds you
Before you crash and burn

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.140
Within the fire
Your soul will rise now

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:49.580
Breathe in, breathe out
Your blank gaze on the brink of life

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:56.380
Step hard on the accelerator now
Escape the tunnel and overtake that pain

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:03.380
A shadow disappears into smoke

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:11.230
Lost light will continue on tomorrow

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:18.360
Someday our world will change
Inside a fantasy Remember, remember

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:25.450
I will mercilessly break your dream
and steal it away, with these hands

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:31.830
Until this body breaks
Beyond the limit We'll never surrender

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.250
Endless agony

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:39.500
Finding my life in the KEMURIKUSA

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.260
Rin-san, can you hear me? Rin-san?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.390
Are you okay, Rin-san?

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.680
My sight is back. My hearing too.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:54.730
So this is the Memory Leaf.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:58.110
How was it? I could hardly see anything.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.530
Were they riding something like this?

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:01.860
Yeah.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:04.700
What is it?

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.860
It was probably you.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.830
Seems like you used to live
with the First Person.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.580
-What?
-Do you remember?

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.620
Huh? Not one bit.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.380
What was I like?

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.340
You were a little different, but not much.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.380
Interesting.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.720
-Like a dolt.
-How mean!

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.430
What else did you find out?

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.050
It's hard to explain.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:31.930
I think you were making islands
with Kemurikusa.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.140
Huh, really?

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:35.730
Oh, but...

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.690
The First Person seemed to
really like you...

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.610
I'm the same.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.160
What are you doing?

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.990
I thought maybe this leaf
makes my face hot.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:56.370
It would get a little better
when I took it out.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.080
You would do that?

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.210
You are no medicine for me, got that?

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.840
Okay...

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.670
Anything about the red tree?

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:10.890
Nothing. But the last Kemurikusa
she made in the end, the color...

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.930
-Do it again. Keep going.
-Okay.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:20.730
Unlocked! So this is the way to do it.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:24.030
Draw lines as if drawing a sprout...

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.990
Don't move it so much.
You're speeding up the view.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.780
Oh, sorry.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:31.410
How's that?

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.620
Wait, let me concentrate.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:34.660
Okay.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.170
What is that...?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:53.470
It's gotten so huge.
We can't let the root reach the lake.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.180
What did you use?

00:14:56.640 --> 00:15:00.140
I connected Daidai and Kiiro to Murasaki.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:02.690
And I made Akairo that way.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:05.690
Murasaki is acting independently.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.820
Wakaba, I...

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.950
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:15.990
I... I...

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:22.040
Don't worry. You did it for me, right?

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.840
You're so kind.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:29.090
I'm sorry. I know that
you're really scared of being all alone.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.510
It's understandable.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.640
I'm sorry I didn't realize earlier.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.060
It's my fault.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.400
It's okay, this happens all the time.

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.530
It's impressive for your first time.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.400
The color is accurate too.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.530
Now, leave the rest to grown-ups.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.330
I'll stop it with a wall,

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:00.910
then fix that area with a big Midori.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:21.230
Huh, seriously?

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.480
Why? It's not moving like a single color.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.980
I made the Akairo
to stop the Kemurikusa

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:30.860
and colors that are a bit off
move together.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:33.360
You really are a genius.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:37.200
Okay, we'll use up this water first then.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:41.410
Midori will keep things as is
or fix the problem. It's perfect.

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.670
Huh?

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:52.380
The fog won't let new ones grow.

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:54.760
Wow, that's totally amazing.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:57.260
I mean, what now?

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:09.820
Are we out of options...?

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:13.400
Oh no, if it drinks up water...

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:16.320
Wakaba...

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:23.960
Wakaba!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.620
Stay there, Riri.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.040
I can probably make it germinate.

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.130
Riri will be saved,
and if all goes well...

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:40.140
I've been feeling well
ever since I met you, Riri.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:44.640
I was amazed at how much energy
earthlings had.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.980
It gave me energy too.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:50.150
And your curiosity is incredible.

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:53.780
Have confidence.
Don't let this get to you.

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:55.820
Wakaba?

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:05.370
We're moving, right? Come on back, hurry!

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:10.380
Actually, I think we're doomed
if I don't use up this water first.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.340
But you can't! Let's run!

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:17.430
Don't worry, we'll be able to meet again.
I think...

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:20.720
And it might take a lot of time.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:22.390
Wakaba!

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:23.930
If I don't make it...

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.730
Do what you like and enjoy your life.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:30.810
Wakaba!

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.380
Wakaba...

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.340
Only grown-ups can open it.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:03.760
I can't open it without Wakaba.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.990
Wakaba is alive. I know he is.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:20.740
He'll come back.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.580
It's been 10 days already, Wakaba.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.020
Rin-san! Run, Rin-san!

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:02.030
I can't just sit here waiting.
Wakaba might be in trouble.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.570
I have to do something. I have to!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:11.500
If only grown-ups can open the wall,
then I'll become one now.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:15.460
Maybe if I use
this Kemurikusa on myself...

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:19.550
The Kemurikusa that
was extracted before printing.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:23.590
It should've been extracted before
it judged whether it was a person or not.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:27.180
That's it, I'll connect
the first part of it and...

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:31.770
If I become a Kemurikusa and not human...

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:37.110
I'll split myself up just in case.
One into the Memory Leaf.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:40.610
I remember Wakaba doing that once. Yes.

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.240
OUR MISSION IS TO SAVE WAKABA.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.910
Wakaba always praised me for this.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:48.160
I'll use what he taught me.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:53.040
There! I did it.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.130
3 consecutive leaves.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:01.210
If it stops during one of them,
I'll disappear...

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:06.430
Even if it does work,
once I become a Kemurikusa,

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.470
that red tree will make me vanish.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:15.020
I'm scared.
I wonder if Wakaba would stop me.

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:18.230
I wouldn't want him to get mad.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.230
But...

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:24.150
I couldn't stand not seeing him again.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.240
What I want to do is...

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.910
save Wakaba!

00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:29.190
I see. The First...

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:30.570
Riri was...
